    <div class="ip-velocity">
      <div class="ip-vcard">
        <span class="ip-status">Planned</span>
        <h3>Vector Velocity</h3>
        <p class="ip-vsize"><b class="ip-num">300B+</b> parameters, planned</p>
        <p>Vector's own coding model. At its planned size it would sit among the largest disclosed coding-tuned models, and, as far as public information shows, the first designed for a workspace that runs several vendors' agents on any model.</p>
        <ul class="ip-clean">
          <li><strong>Designed for Vector's loop:</strong> planning, tool calls, edits, checks and verification, across the specialists and the review pass.</li>
          <li><strong>Planned to sell in the open:</strong> one choice in the picker beside 219 providers, measured by the same tokenomics. Through Codium its steps would count in tokens and Codium credits, like every Codium model's, not in dollars, so it would have to win on measured results.</li>
          <li><strong>Planned to run through Codium,</strong> so model spend that goes to other labs today could go to Vector's own model.</li>
          <li><strong>Not trained on customers' code.</strong> There are no weights or benchmarks yet, so this page makes no performance claims for it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="ip-why-us">
        <div class="ip-eyebrow">Why Vector can build it</div>
        <div class="ip-why-item"><h4>It controls the harness</h4><p>Vector maintains its agent, its tools and its eight specialists, so the loop the model is trained for is known, not a guess about someone else's product. Cursor and Cognition took the same route: their own models, trained inside their own agents.</p></div>
        <div class="ip-why-item"><h4>It already measures cost per task</h4><p>Vector prices each session from provider-reported tokens wherever the model has a price, and an offline benchmark prices every request. Velocity would be measured with the same tools as every other model.</p></div>
        <div class="ip-why-item"><h4>It has the channel</h4><p>Velocity would ship into a free workspace on desktop and in the terminal, and sell through Codium, with no new product for anyone to adopt.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
